ex:A_backup_instance_of_slurmdbd_can_be_configured_by_specifying_AccountingStorageBackupHost_in_slurm_conf_as_well_as_DbdBackupHost_in_slurmdbd_conf_The_backup_host_should_be_on_a_different_machine_than_the_one_hosting_the_primary_instance_of_slurmdbd_Both_instances_of_slurmdbd_should_have_access_to_the_same_database_share_the_same_munge_key_s_and_have_the_same_users_with_the_same_UID_GIDs_The_network_page_has_a_visual_representation_of_how_this_might_look a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "A backup instance of slurmdbd can be configured by specifying AccountingStorageBackupHost in slurm.conf, as well as DbdBackupHost in slurmdbd.conf. The backup host should be on a different machine than the one hosting the primary instance of slurmdbd. Both instances of slurmdbd should have access to the same database, share the same munge key(s), and have the same users with the same UID/GIDs. The network page has a visual representation of how this might look." .

