    rdfs:label "Note that SlurmDBD relies upon existing Slurm plugins for authentication and Slurm SQL for database use, but the other Slurm commands and daemons are not required on the host where SlurmDBD is installed. Install the slurm and slurm-slurmdbd RPMs on the server where SlurmDBD is to run." .

ex:Note_that_for_single_task_processes_TresUsageInTot_could_be_used_as_the_maximum_memory_that_the_step_consumed_at_any_time_which_will_be_equal_to_MaxRSS_and_effectively_represent_the_step_memory_peak_Profiling_works_similarly_and_we_provide_plugins_like_HDF5_and_InfluxDB_that_can_help_to_visualize_accounting_data_in_other_ways a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Note that for single task processes, TresUsageInTot could be used as the maximum memory that the step consumed at any time, which will be equal to MaxRSS and effectively represent the step memory peak. Profiling works similarly, and we provide plugins like HDF5 and InfluxDB that can help to visualize accounting data in other ways." .

