ex:When_using_a_SelectType_of_select_cons_tres_the_default_allocation_method_across_nodes_is_block_allocation_allocate_all_available_CPUs_in_a_node_before_using_another_node_The_default_allocation_method_within_a_node_is_cyclic_allocation_allocate_available_CPUs_in_a_round_robin_fashion_across_the_sockets_within_a_node_Users_may_override_the_default_behavior_using_the_appropriate_command_line_options_described_below_The_choice_of_allocation_methods_may_influence_which_specific_CPUs_are_allocated_to_the_job_step a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "When using a SelectType of select/cons_tres, the default allocation method across nodes is block allocation (allocate all available CPUs in a node before using another node). The default allocation method within a node is cyclic allocation (allocate available CPUs in a round-robin fashion across the sockets within a node). Users may override the default behavior using the appropriate command line options described below. The choice of allocation methods may influence which specific CPUs are allocated to the job/step." .

